@startuml TBOT-Auth
title Domain · auth — identity & session
left to right direction

actor Guest
actor "Authenticated User" as AuthUser
actor "Google OAuth" as Google <<external>>
actor "Apple Sign-In" as Apple <<external>>

package "auth" {
  usecase "Sign Up (email)"          as UC_AUTH_SIGNUP
  usecase "Log In (email)"           as UC_AUTH_LOGIN
  usecase "Continue with Google"     as UC_AUTH_GOOGLE
  usecase "Continue with Apple"      as UC_AUTH_APPLE
  usecase "Reset Password"           as UC_AUTH_RESET <<UNDEFINED>>
  usecase "Recover Login Error"      as UC_AUTH_ERR
  usecase "Set Up Child Profile"     as UC_AUTH_CHILD
  usecase "Refresh Token"            as UC_AUTH_REFRESH <<UNDEFINED>>
  usecase "Logout"                   as UC_AUTH_LOGOUT <<UNDEFINED>>
}

Guest    --> UC_AUTH_SIGNUP
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_LOGIN
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_GOOGLE
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_APPLE
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_RESET
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_ERR
Guest    --> UC_AUTH_CHILD
AuthUser --> UC_AUTH_REFRESH
AuthUser --> UC_AUTH_LOGOUT

UC_AUTH_GOOGLE ..> Google : <<delegate>>
UC_AUTH_APPLE  ..> Apple  : <<delegate>>

note bottom of UC_AUTH_RESET
  Button only — target = onb_login.
  No reset API observed in source.
end note

' [exit] success → kid-hub (UC_HUB_VIEW)
' Files: src/features/auth/LoginPage.jsx, src/features/auth/ChildProfilePage.jsx
' Store: src/store/auth.store.js
@enduml
